&lt;p&gt;Cribl is seeking a FP&amp;amp;A Systems and AI Enablement Manager, to join our finance team. Reporting to the Director of Corporate FP&amp;amp;A, this role goes far beyond traditional system administration. We are looking for a hands-on architect who will build next-generation financial systems and actively deploy artificial intelligence to eliminate manual workflows. As a key partner to finance leadership, you will drive the planning, forecasting, and reporting processes that power our organization&#39;s growth as we transition to a public company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As An Active Member Of Our Team, You Will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own our EPM platform (Pigment): &lt;/strong&gt;Manage the system end-to-end, including data models, calculation logic, dimensional structure, security architecture, and release management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate Business to Tech: &lt;/strong&gt;Convert complex business requirements (revenue models, headcount plans, unit economics) into technical platform solutions and scalable modeling patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Architecture: &lt;/strong&gt;Make foundational architectural decisions that will determine how planning functions across the company for years to come.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Finance AI Adoption: &lt;/strong&gt;Identify, pilot, and deploy AI use cases, including automated variance commentary, narrative generation, anomaly detection, and AI-assisted scenario modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate Workflows:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and test conversational and agent-driven finance workflows that guide business partners through routine planning tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate on Deployment:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Data Science and IT to roll out AI solutions, ensuring strict governance, accuracy, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are a remote-first company and work happens across many time-zones – you may be required to occasionally perform duties outside your standard working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;If You’ve Got It - We Want It&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Information Systems, Accounting, Economics, or another data-related focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating at a high-growth, pre-IPO SaaS company is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python or similar scripting languages is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 5+ years in a hybrid FP&amp;amp;A/Systems role, possessing a strong foundation in corporate finance and a deep understanding of the business logic behind financial forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Chops: Deep, hands-on implementation experience in modern EPMs (Pigment Certified Modeler credentials are a plus), with exposure to cross-system integrations (e.g., Workday, NetSuite, Salesforce, BI tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Fluency: Active, daily utilization of LLMs, copilots, and automation tools to solve real business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soft Skills: Sharp attention to detail, exceptional organizational skills, and the ability to navigate ambiguity while wearing multiple hats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Management: Exceptional communication skills with a proven track record of influencing key stakeholders, driving alignment, and working cross-functionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
